msgid "Generate Descriptions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:249
msgid "Saves, as written descriptions, the meta description each post already publishes when none was written: the one generated from its content. The page does not change; the description just stops depending on the content staying as it is. Posts with a description of their own are left alone. Up to 100 posts per call."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:289
msgid "Taxonomy, such as category, post_tag, or a custom one like a brand or a product category. Only public taxonomies with archives have SEO fields."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:299
msgid "List Term SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:300
msgid "Lists the terms of the taxonomies with SEO fields — categories, tags, brands, product categories — with the title and description their archive publishes, whether a title or description was written, noindex, and how many posts each has. Filter by taxonomy and by what is missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:314
msgid "Only terms without a written title, or without a written description."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:331
msgid "Get Term SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:332
msgid "Returns the SEO of a term's archive page — a category, tag, brand or product category: its URL, the search title and meta description it publishes, the ones written for it, noindex and whether it is in the sitemap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:353
msgid "Update Term SEO"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-abilities.php:354
msgid "Updates the SEO of a term's archive page; only the fields you send. As with posts, the title is the full title, printed as written: the site name is not added. noindex keeps the archive out of search results and the sitemap. Returns what the archive now publishes, with warnings when a title or description may be cut (over 70 or 165 characters)."
msgstr ""

