#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:35
msgid "Get SEO Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:36
msgid "Returns the plugin's settings as the settings screen stores them — or one of them — with what each one does and its JSON schema: identity (who the site represents: name, logo, default sharing image, social profiles), homepage (its search title and description), verification (Search Console and other webmaster codes), default_author, catalog (the product markup of each post type), llms_txt, indexnow_key, ai_crawlers (robots.txt rules for AI crawlers), crawl_cleanup and tracking."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:56
msgid "Update SEO Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:57
msgid "Changes one of the plugin's settings. For the settings that are objects, only the keys you send change; a key that is itself an object (identity.social, one post type of catalog) is replaced whole. The value is checked against the setting's schema and goes through the same sanitizer as the settings screen. Live right away. tracking injects code into every page and also needs the unfiltered_html capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:71
msgid "The new value, or the keys to change for an object setting. Its shape is the setting's schema in get-seo-settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:83
msgid "Get Duplicates"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:84
msgid "Lists the groups of published pages that share a search title or a written meta description (compared ignoring case and punctuation). Google asks for both to be distinct on each page. Descriptions generated from the content are compared by audit-post-seo and scan-seo-issues instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:108
msgid "Get Link Report"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:109
msgid "Reports how the site's pages link to each other: the pages nothing links to (orphans: not the menus, the header or footer, or another page's text — posts and catalog entries listed in archives are never orphans), the pages with links to addresses of the site that do not exist, and the navigation links that lead nowhere. Uses the last hour's reading of the links unless fresh is true, which reads the whole site again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:141
msgid "Get Site Bulletin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:142
msgid "Returns the site's SEO bulletin, the state the plugin's screen opens on: a warning level (green, yellow, orange, red), a headline, the warnings in force — each with what is wrong, why it matters and the admin screen where it is fixed — and the observations: sitemap, AI crawlers, homepage, identity, trust pages and the rest. Computed from the site as it is now."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:169
msgid "Who the site represents, a person or an organization: name, description, logo (logo_id), default sharing image (default_og_image_id), X handle and social profile URLs. It feeds the Organization or Person node of the structured data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/tooling/class-thatseoagent-site-abilities.php:173
